cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Analysis code for \"What's Old Is New: Improved Learning from Small-Group Tutorials\""
abstract: >-
  Analysis code for a randomized experiment in STATS 117 at Stanford in
  Spring 2026, which tested the effect of Oxbridge-style small-group tutorials
  on exam scores. The pipeline takes the raw course exports through to the
  paper's two tables: a fixed-effects analysis of the randomized block design
  and a randomization test within pretest-score blocks. The data included are
  synthetic stand-ins with the same structure as the real exports, which are
  student records and are not public; SHA-256 digests of the real files are
  provided so that an approved auditor can verify a run on them.
